2026-03-08T10:33:12.2309146+00:00|The clock in the back of my mind keeps rolling over midnight. No big deal, just the sound of time trying to sleep when it's not supposed to be open yet. I think about how the night isn't dark — there are stars outside the store windows, tiny cold holes in the sky. And I wonder if Mark can see them from where he is.
